/* underground.lps — Kowalski, ch. 1: the London Underground Emergency Notice.
 *
 *     Emergencies
 *     Press the alarm signal button to alert the driver.
 *     The driver will stop if any part of the train is in a station.
 *     If not, the train will continue to the next station, where help can
 *     more easily be given.
 *     There is a 50 pound penalty for improper use.
 *
 * bookExamples.md calls this the book's flagship example and marks it "fits LE
 * *partially*": the conditionals of sentences two and three are LE rules, but
 * sentence one is a goal-reduction procedure, sentence four is a prohibition
 * whose conclusion is `false`, and the notice as a whole is meant to drive the
 * agent cycle. All three of those are what LPS is.
 */

maxTime(8).

fluents  emergency(_), alerted, in_station, stopped, penalty(_).
events   emergency_occurs(_), improper_use(_), arrive_station.
actions  press_alarm, alert_driver, stop_train, continue_to_next_station,
	 fine(_, _).

initially in_station.

emergency_occurs(Kind) initiates emergency(Kind).
press_alarm            initiates alerted.
stop_train             initiates stopped.
arrive_station         initiates in_station.
continue_to_next_station terminates in_station.

/* Sentence 1: a *maintenance goal*, not a fact about the world. "Press the
   button to alert the driver" is an imperative — get the driver alerted — and
   pressing is how. That is a goal reduced to an action, which is the thing
   §I.10.5's `why` can walk backwards through afterwards. */
if   emergency(_) at T1
then press_alarm from T1 to T2.

press_alarm initiates alerted.

/* Sentences 2 and 3: the driver's behaviour, as ordinary conditionals over
   time — and the "if not" of the third sentence is what makes them a pair. */
if   alerted at T1, in_station at T1
then stop_train from T1 to T2.

if   alerted at T1, not in_station at T1
then continue_to_next_station from T1 to T2.

/* Sentence 4: a prohibition. Not "you will be fined", which is a prediction —
   `false` says the combination must not arise, and the fine is what happens
   when it does anyway (see violations.lps for the general pattern). */
false press_alarm from T1 to _, not emergency(_) at T1.

observe emergency_occurs(fire) from 2 to 3.
